WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.710 --> 00:00:09.030
It sounds like a cliche but the one word
keeping chief executives up at night is

00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:14.040
disruption. If you're the CEO of a big
company all it takes to get you paranoid

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:18.810
is to hear that Amazon is about to
invest in your sector. For example when

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:22.800
Amazon acquired online pharmacy PillPack for less than a billion dollars

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:27.740
last year leading brick-and-mortar
rivals Walgreens and CVS instantly lost

00:00:27.740 --> 00:00:33.660
11 billion dollars in market value. So
it's no surprise that CVS spent 69

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:37.880
billion dollars to buy health insurer
Aetna. Why do they do that?

00:00:37.880 --> 00:00:41.399
It was a clear response to Amazon's
plans to enter the business of selling

00:00:41.399 --> 00:00:46.710
prescription drugs online. The fear that
Amazon or other tech giant's such as

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:52.350
Google, Facebook, Apple or even Uber can
muscle their way into any sector is

00:00:52.350 --> 00:00:58.260
forcing legacy companies to take risky
bets on big acquisitions. That's the only

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:03.329
way they can stay relevant and fight the
disruptors. For example, IBM made its

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:07.799
biggest acquisition in its 107 year
history by buying an open-source

00:01:07.799 --> 00:01:12.030
software company called Red Hat for
thirty four billion dollars the logic of

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:16.890
this deal is very simple. The lucrative
cloud computing business is dominated by

00:01:16.890 --> 00:01:22.350
Amazon Web Services and Google if IBM
wanted to catch up in this business it

00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:27.090
needed to make a big acquisition. The
other big disruptor has been Netflix the

00:01:27.090 --> 00:01:32.159
TV streaming company has forced a number
of telecom and media companies to forge

00:01:32.159 --> 00:01:37.650
new alliances to stay relevant in their
businesses. Boring telecom company AT&amp;T

00:01:37.650 --> 00:01:41.700
agreed to pay a hundred and eight
billion dollars to buy Time Warner

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:46.680
that's the owner of HBO and CNN. Last
year Disney and Comcast entered into a

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:51.299
bidding war to buy most of Rupert
Murdoch's 21st Century Fox. At the end

00:01:51.299 --> 00:01:58.290
disney prevailed but still comcast ended
up buying european broadcaster Sky. We

00:01:58.290 --> 00:02:02.159
should expect more of these kinds of
deals. Cash is cheap due to historically

00:02:02.159 --> 00:02:06.600
low interest rates and many companies
have a ton of extra cash on their

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:10.950
balance sheet thanks to Donald Trump's
corporate tax cuts. This tax bill is

00:02:10.950 --> 00:02:13.890
incredible. The conditions to make big
deals

00:02:13.890 --> 00:02:16.550
are as good as ever.

